Source: bbb-plugin-remote-desktop
Section: web
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), nodejs, npm

Package: bbb-plugin-remote-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: BigBlueButton remote desktop plugin
 Adds VNC remote desktop sharing to BigBlueButton v3.0 via the
 plugin architecture. Moderators can share a VNC desktop in the
 presentation area; participants see and (optionally) interact with
 it through their browser. No core BBB modifications required.

Package: bbb-wss-proxy
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-websockify, nginx
Description: WebSocket-to-VNC proxy with BigBlueButton session-token auth
 A websockify wrapper that authenticates incoming WebSocket
 connections against BigBlueButton's own session-token API
 (/bigbluebutton/api/enter) before relaying them to a backend VNC
 server.
 .
 Pairs with bbb-plugin-remote-desktop, which appends each user's
 BBB session token as ?sessionToken=... to the WebSocket URL. Any
 user authenticated to a meeting therefore reaches the proxy with
 valid credentials — no separate sign-in.
 .
 An optional ALLOWED_TARGETS regex lets the caller pick a VNC
 backend by query parameter (default: relay everything to
 localhost:5900).
